&lt;p&gt;    This is for kerberos enabled environment, correct ?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15836124" author="githubbot" created="Tue, 24 Jan 2017 13:23:44 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user zjffdu commented on the issue:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/1938&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/1938&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    No, impersonation works in both secured and unsecured enviroment. Without this PR, we still pass proxy-user `anonymous` to livy server. And this cause we launch the spark app via user `anonymous`. But it should the user `livy` in the anonymous mode. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
